# Mob programs from the fixture area that go wrong, with only area_update running, in the temple (3001): the
# broken golem (30004) and the herald (30000), with Decimus (10).
# - ping: pong; iffy: an if never closed, which does no harm
# - dollar: if-checks with the wrong words (a missing comparison, a missing actor, a bad $-code, a word that isn't
#   a comparison) log a bug each, count as false, and the program goes on
# - elsewhere, endless, orphan, nested: an else, endif or or without an if, and ifs nested past 12, each log a bug
#   and end the program without counting the call off (sic, #87); ping still answers after four of them
# - bogus: an if-check that doesn't exist, the fifth; now every mob program in the game is past MAX_CALL_LEVEL:
#   ping, also and the herald's greeting do nothing
@place mobprog.are mobprog.are
@place area-mobprog.lst area.lst
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@mob 30004 3001
@mob 30000 3001
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
say ping
say iffy
say dollar
say elsewhere
say endless
say orphan
say nested
say ping
say bogus
say ping
say also
south
north
@state
